{"id": "EUVD-2026-91480", "enisaUuid": "30108097-c552-3752-a015-9117c841fe76", "description": "YesWiki before 4.6.7 contains a session fixation vulnerability that allows attackers to hijack authenticated sessions because login does not regenerate the PHP session ID. Attackers who set or learn a victim's pre-authentication YesWiki-* session cookie can reuse it after login to access private content and perform actions with the victim's privileges.", "datePublished": "2026-10-02T11:38:34", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-06T16:20:33", "baseScore": 7.6, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:H/AT:P/PR:N/UI:P/VC:H/VI:H/VA:N/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://github.com/YesWiki/yeswiki/security/advisories/GHSA-7fvc-v2hp-5pwh", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/yeswiki-before-4.6.7-session-fixation-via-login-in-authcontroller-php"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-104469", "GHSA-c9hw-c2mv-jj5c"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.23, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "d95aa383-b903-3cb6-9824-37b61e5c398b", "product": {"name": "yeswiki", "vendor": {"name": "YesWiki"}}, "product_version": "0 <4.6.7"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "d2badc8f-faeb-3025-85fb-3828863e8c3a", "vendor": {"name": "YesWiki"}}], "isExploited": false}